<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's WestLB cuts prime rate to 23.95 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary's WestLB cuts prime rate to 23.95 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Westdeutche Landesbank (Hungaria) Rt said on Wednesday that it will reduce its prime lending rate on forint loans to 23.95 percent from 24.50 percent.</p>
<p>The reduction is effective November 1, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>WestLB's current prime rate has been effective since October 7 when the bank reduced it to 24.50 percent from 25.00 percent.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
